const uint8_t gm_s5068[5659] = "usage: gamma <command> [options] <file>\012\012commands:\012  lex     print the tokens of source files\012  parse   check the syntax of source files (--dump prints the syntax tree)\012  modules load a program's modules without checking them and print the module graph\012  decls   resolve a program's declarations without checking bodies and print them\012  tir     check a program and print the typed program the checker produces\012  check   type-check a program (a .gm file or a module directory)\012  doc     write the API documentation of a module as Markdown or HTML (gamma doc --help)\012  lint    check a package with its tests and report the findings of the lint rules\012  fix     check a program and apply the fixes its diagnostics suggest\012  build   compile a program to a native executable via the system C compiler\012  run     compile a program via C and run it, or run it in the interpreter (--backend=interp);\012          arguments after the file go to the program\012  test    run the test declarations of a module and of the modules of its package\012          that it imports, compiled into one executable via C\012  bench   run the bench declarations the same way and report the time per run\012          (compiled in fast mode unless --mode is given)\012  new, init, fetch, update, add, remove, cache\012          the package manager (gamma help)\012  fmt     format source files in place: gamma fmt [--check] <file or directory>... (\"-\" filters stdin to stdout)\012  repl    interactive read-eval-print loop on the interpreter: gamma repl [--quiet] [file]\012          (loads the file's declarations)\012  lsp     run the language server on standard input and output\012  help    print this message\012  version print the compiler version\012\012options:\012  --diag-format=human|short|json\012                              how to print diagnostics (default: human)\012  --quiet                     (repl) no banner and prompts, even on a terminal\012  --recover                   (lex, parse) lex with the layout recovery tools use after errors\012  --dump                      (parse) print the syntax tree\012  --mode=debug|checked|safe|fast\012                              (build, run, test, bench, repl) the build mode (default: debug); safe builds\012                              with Fil-C\012  --target=<triple>           (check, build, run, test, bench) the target (default: the C compiler's)\012  -g                          (build, run) add debug information that maps the executable back to the\012                              Gamma source (build also writes the lldb formatters, gamma_lldb.py,\012                              next to the executable)\012  -o <file>                   (build) the executable to write (default: the input's name)\012  --emit-c                    (build) stop after writing the C file (<exe>.c)\012  --filter=<text>             (test, bench) run only the tests whose name or module path\012                              contains <text>\012  --all                       (test, bench) also run those of the modules of the package\012                              that nothing imports (every directory with .gm files)\012  --package=<name>            (test, bench) run those of the dependency <name> of the input's\012                              package (or of one of its dependencies) instead, with the\012                              dependency versions this package locks\012  --show-output               (test, bench) also print the output of the tests that pass\012  --jobs=<n>, -j <n>          (test) run <n> tests at a time (default 1; 0: one per processor;\012                              the output is still in order)\012  --timeout=<seconds>         (test, bench) fail a test that runs longer than <seconds> (no\012                              limit by default)\012  --time                      (test, bench) print how long each test took and the total\012  --coverage[=<file>]         (test) count the lines of the package that the tests run; print\012                              a table, and with <file> write LCOV\012  --backend=c|interp          (run) compile via C (the default) or run in the interpreter;\012                              (test, bench) only c is accepted\012  --offline                   (check, run, build) never use the network for dependencies\012  --locked                    (check, run, build) fail if gamma.lock is missing or out of date\012  --profile=<name>            (check, run, build) use the [profile.<name>] table of gamma.toml\012  --fix                       (lint) apply the fixes of the warnings that have one\012  --rules                     (lint) list the rules and their default levels\012  --allow=<rules>, --warn=<rules>, --deny=<rules>\012                              (lint) set the level of rules (comma-separated; all is every rule)\012  -D, --deny-warnings         (lint) report every rule that would warn as an error\012\012environment:\012  GAMMA_STD      the standard library (default: lib/gamma/std next to bin/)\012  GAMMA_CORE     the core library (default: core next to the standard library)\012  GAMMA_RUNTIME  the runtime's C sources (default: runtime two levels above the standard library)\012  CC             the C compiler (default: cc), with its arguments\012  CFLAGS         flags for every C compile, LDFLAGS flags for the link (after those of gamma.toml)\012  GAMMA_CACHE_DIR\012                 the package store (default: the user's cache directory; empty turns it off)\012  GAMMA_C_UNITS  the number of C units of a Debug build (default: by size and processors)\012  GAMMA_RUNNER   the program that runs the executables of another target (e.g. qemu-s390x)\012  WASI_SDK_PATH  the WASI SDK (for wasm32-wasi; its clang is the default C compiler there)\012  WASM_OPT       the wasm-opt program (default: wasm-opt) for programs that use fibers\012\012";
